title The grade that was remembered, and the measurement that was two points lower
prompt Continue the diffuser lane; the previous lap was cut mid-send with its whole build parked in a stash.
rota lap 4679, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; read foundations/20260905-154954_the-clock-and-the-mark.md, whose count-never-number discipline has a sibling this lap met -- grade, never recall
think The round-open named four parked files under stash@{0} and the claim board read capability-lattice seat=diffuser status=building mine, so the lap was a recovery rather than a new build: the work existed and had never reached a commit.
think git stash pop restored fourteen files and conflicted on three pins, each for its own reason. construction/fleet-claims.kyri conflicted because the parked side had CLOSED my claim while upstream had since opened copal's beside it; I took upstream whole, since the claim stays open until this send lands it.
think construction/standing-equipment.kyri conflicted between two guard blocks that are not rivals -- upstream's lint_table_runs and my capability_lattice -- so both were kept and the roster reads 355 guards.
think construction/ITINERARY.md carried two conflicts. The Git nib is rewritten at every send, so upstream's stood. The card body needed a real merge: the parked side held my NEW block beside petrichor's ELDER one, upstream the reverse, so the resolution is my new DIFFUSER block followed by upstream's newer PETRICHOR block.
think Before believing any of it I ran the witness on metal rather than trusting the parked claim: 59 legs, faults=0, three mutations bitten, control_verdict=ok. The live scan agrees with the card entry figure for figure -- masks_seated=10, seated_incomparable_unordered=32, seated_over_admitted=48, seated_under_admitted=0, rights_headroom=3.
obs THE FINDING IS A NUMBER THAT WAS RECALLED RATHER THAN READ. The card, the paper's own file line, and the parked log's status field all said the paper graded A 93. Run this lap, qa_report_card answers register=70, reach=100, truth=100, service=95, composite=91 -- A 91. Two points, in three places, written by a hand that had run the tool.
obs A grade is a MEASUREMENT and it wears the same hazard the rota's own row-4 page names for a count: typed into prose it is held by nobody, and it drifts on the first edit nobody re-runs. The paper's register reading sits at exactly the Field ceiling -- 30% of 68 sentences -- so a single added negative sentence would have moved the letter while the prose still claimed the elder figure.
obs What holds it: nothing. qa_report_card is a command rather than a gate, and no roster row reads a grade a document claims about itself against the tool's own answer. That is a meter a later lap could build -- a page naming its own grade is a checkable promise -- and it is named here rather than built, since this lap's allocation belongs to landing the parked work.
obs I EDITED THE CARD WHILE THE PASS WAS READING IT, which the card's own Standing block forbids in four words -- holding still while it runs. The pass closed `tree_moved=yes` and `roster_receipt_write=withheld_guard_red`, so it earned no receipt, and two of its three reds were already repaired by the time it printed them. The repair cost nothing here because the reds were mine and the fix was right; the cost it could carry is a reading nobody can attribute to a tree.
obs A stale roster lock stood from the cut lap, pid 3206189 at launch_head 941d26d3e0, its verdict already fixed at tree_moved. The runner named the pid and the TERM form itself; I resolved /proc/3206189/cwd to this tree before signaling, and the lock released one guard later exactly as the runner said it would.
obs THE SAME CLASS FIRED TWICE, AND THE SECOND HALF WAS A HASH. The hot roster pass read two
reds, `nib_honesty` and `remember_git_nib`, on one root: the card's Git nib field read
`73c0c81159` and the commit it names is `73c0c81157`. One digit, typed rather than read from
`git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD~1`, and the hash resolved to nothing. Both guards went GREEN on
the corrected field. So the lap's finding is not about grades: a number a hand types is held by
nobody, and this tree already walls the hash and reads nothing over the grade.
